module_specs:
  video_timing: |
    Count 1650 pixel clocks per line and 750 lines per frame. Use 1280 active
    pixels and 720 active lines, with horizontal front porch/sync/back porch
    values of 110/40/220 and vertical values of 5/5/20. Generate positive
    horizontal and vertical syncs and assert frame_end once per frame.
  color_bars: |
    For pattern 0, generate eight 160-pixel-wide vertical bars ordered white,
    yellow, cyan, green, magenta, red, blue, black. The active qualification
    comes from video_timing. Other pattern numbers are handled according to
    assumption A-1.
  median_filter: |
    Compute the median independently for red, green, and blue over each 3 x 3
    neighbourhood. At active-picture boundaries, replicate the nearest active
    picture pixel. Delay the picture qualification and both sync signals so
    that they remain aligned with the filtered picture.
  frame_counter: |
    Reset to zero and increment its unsigned 32-bit count once on each frame_end.
  video_cdc: |
    Synchronize pattern selection from clk_sys into clk_pix. Transfer the
    changing frame count from clk_pix into clk_sys using a CDC scheme suitable
    for a multi-bit counter, such as Gray-code synchronization.
  video_control: |
    The shell owns the USB-UART and register window. Place PATTERN at offset
    0x00 and FRAME_COUNT at offset 0x04 relative to window_base 0x00, which
    corresponds to addresses in the shell's 0x80-0xFF window. Support the
    newline-terminated ASCII ID?, PAT n, and FRAME? commands with line-terminated
    responses. PAT command behavior beyond the specified bars follows
    assumption A-1.
  video_output: |
    Forward the filtered syncs. Forward filtered RGB only when active is true,
    BTNC is not pressed, and the pixel-clock lock indication is asserted;
    otherwise drive all colour channels to zero.

  top: |
    Connect video_timing coordinates and active qualification to color_bars.
    Connect the selected pattern through video_control and video_cdc to
    color_bars. Connect the colour channels and timing qualifiers through
    median_filter, then connect its outputs to video_output. Connect
    video_timing.frame_end to frame_counter.frame_end; pass the counter through
    video_cdc to video_control. Drive LED[0] from clk_pix.locked.

requirements:
  - id: S-1
    text: "Generate 1280 x 720, 60 Hz video timing with a 74.25 MHz pixel clock, 1650 pixel clocks per line (1280 active, 110 front porch, 40 sync, 220 back porch), 750 lines per frame (720 active, 5 front porch, 5 sync, 20 back porch), and positive horizontal and vertical sync."
    proof: [simulation, hardware, analysis]
    modules: [video_timing, top]
  - id: S-2
    text: "By default, generate eight vertical colour bars, each 160 active pixels wide, in this order: white, yellow, cyan, green, magenta, red, blue, black."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [color_bars, video_control, top]
  - id: S-3
    text: "For each output pixel, compute the median independently for each colour channel over the pixel's 3 x 3 neighbourhood."
    proof: [simulation, formal]
    modules: [median_filter, top]
  - id: S-4
    text: "Keep the output picture and sync signals aligned to the video timing that would be produced without the median filter."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [median_filter, video_output, top]
  - id: S-5
    text: "Drive all colour outputs to zero outside the active picture, while BTNC is pressed, or while the pixel clock is not stable."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [video_output, top]
  - id: S-6
    text: "Light LED[0] when the pixel clock is stable."
    proof: [hardware]
    modules: [top]
  - id: S-7
    text: "Provide a USB-UART test shell at 115200 baud with design ID VMED that allows a host to choose the pattern and read a frame counter."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [video_control, top]

